usage: benchmark_raw_batch.py [-h] --cli CLI --input-dir INPUT_DIR --manifest
                              MANIFEST --single-home SINGLE_HOME --mesh-home
                              MESH_HOME --scratch SCRATCH --report REPORT
                              --plugin PLUGIN --worker WORKER
                              [--trials TRIALS] [--jobs JOBS]
                              [--tile-edge TILE_EDGE] [--timeout TIMEOUT]

Time complete RAW dehaze batches on one local executor and an explicitly
paired mesh. The input manifest is a JSON object mapping relative RAW paths to
SHA-256. The profiles must already be running. Each timed invocation uses a
fresh output directory on the same volume. Reports contain file names and peer
identifiers.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --cli CLI
  --input-dir INPUT_DIR
  --manifest MANIFEST
  --single-home SINGLE_HOME
  --mesh-home MESH_HOME
  --scratch SCRATCH
  --report REPORT
  --plugin PLUGIN
  --worker WORKER       full remote peer ID, repeat per worker
  --trials TRIALS
  --jobs JOBS
  --tile-edge TILE_EDGE
  --timeout TIMEOUT     per-batch wall time limit in seconds
